diagram='''<svg role="img" aria-label="Unstressed flight, contact, then compression yield or removal, followed by scoped archive checks" viewBox="0 0 1050 170"><g fill="#172e41" stroke="#3d667d"><rect x="5" y="30" width="235" height="110" rx="8"/><rect x="275" y="30" width="225" height="110" rx="8"/><rect x="535" y="30" width="235" height="110" rx="8"/><rect x="805" y="30" width="240" height="110" rx="8"/></g><g stroke="#68cbbd" stroke-width="3"><path d="M240 85H275M500 85H535M770 85H805"/></g><g fill="#e1edf5" font-family="system-ui" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17"><text x="122" y="60">Two-mass flight</text><text x="387" y="60">Native collision</text><text x="652" y="60">Later beam changes</text><text x="925" y="60">Verified observations</text></g><g fill="#a9c0d0" font-family="system-ui" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14"><text x="122" y="93">5 m/s, rest = 1 m</text><text x="122" y="119">Zero initial beam load</text><text x="387" y="93">Tick 5202 / 2.601 s</text><text x="387" y="119">Actual force accumulator</text><text x="652" y="93">Yield 5210 / removal 5284</text><text x="652" y="119">Strength loss from 5978</text><text x="925" y="93">12,001 dense frames</text><text x="925" y="119">Local law + ledger parity</text></g></svg>'''
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{x}</td>' for x in [s['scenario'],s['timeline']['firstContactTick'],s['timeline']['firstParameterTick'] or 'none',s['timeline']['firstStrengthTick'] or 'none',s['timeline']['firstRemovalTick'] or 'none',s['timeline']['parameterChanges'],s['timeline']['strengthChanges'],s['timeline']['removed']])+'</tr>' for s in selected)
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Slice 07 · later impact transitions</title>',style,'</head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">RIGS OF RODS TRIALS · SLICE 07 · 10 OCTOBER 2026 · DEV</div><h1>Collision first.<br>Beam transitions afterward.</h1><p class="lead">Two source-built native impact fixtures now qualify later compressive yield, tensile strength loss and beam removal, with complete force/contact/beam capture and an observed workbench timeline.</p>',diagram]
parts+=['<div class="notice">Scoped Passed validates these pinned native rules, local integration and archive agreement. It does not certify real vehicle materials, calibrated fracture dissipation or a fully independent predicted trajectory. Vehicle science remains NotReady and the prior observer-overhead target remains unmet.</div>','<h2>The experiment and measured sequence</h2><p>Two 100 kg moving nodes share one normal beam (k=10,000 N/m, c=0, rest=1 m, strength=2,000 N). Two 1 kg anchors are fixed; the other two beams are disabled. Both moving nodes start at 5 m/s with zero extension, gravity, drag and wind. A native box front face at x=514 m is 13 m ahead of the initial front. Observation lasts 7 physics seconds. Yield uses ±200 N bounds and coefficient 0.25; removal uses high yield bounds.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Fixture</th><th>Contact tick</th><th>First parameter</th><th>First strength</th><th>First removal</th><th>Parameter count</th><th>Strength count</th><th>Removed</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+rows+'</tbody></table></div><p>Compressive yield starts 4 ms after contact; tensile weakening starts 388 ms after contact. The removal fixture breaks 41 ms after contact. Neither changes a beam at tick 1. The yield fixture ends with rest '+f"{selected[0]['finalRestM']:.9f}"+' m and strength '+f"{selected[0]['finalStrengthN']:.6f}"+' N.</p>',image('collision-state.png','Unaltered physics values from independently CRC-decoded every-step detail; strength is a native model parameter, not a calibrated material measure.'),image('energy-state.png','Native moving-node kinetic energy and supported linear spring storage. A storage drop or contact work is not measured material dissipation.')]
parts+=['<h2>Force and storage accounting</h2><p>Both fixtures peak at 800,000.1875 N net barrier force. Independent dense decoding reproduces native contact counts, peaks and signed X impulses: yield '+f"{selected[0]['detail']['barrierImpulseNs'][0]:.9f}"+' N·s; removal '+f"{selected[1]['detail']['barrierImpulseNs'][0]:.9f}"+' N·s. Aggregate/dense force, momentum and kinetic-energy reductions match exactly.</p><p>Yield rest-storage ports sum to '+f"{selected[0]['restPortJ']:.6f}"+' J; the removal storage port is '+f"{selected[1]['removalPortJ']:.6f}"+' J. These signed ports remove/change modeled elastic storage once. Native constitutive correction and actual consumed versus generated forces remain separately attributed. Contact midpoint work uses actual node kicks; none of these values is relabeled as fracture energy.</p>', '<h2>What the qualification establishes</h2><p>The double-precision reference is driven by recorded local beam lengths and contact inputs. It independently recomputes native yield/correction/strength/removal rules and one-dimensional contact reaction; checks rest/strength continuity, endpoint force writes, carried versus generated epochs, kick-drift steps, aggregate/detail parity, event identity and signed storage ports. It requires actual precontact history and the appropriate outcome strictly after consumed contact. This is a local model-conformance check, not an independent long-horizon collision-time oracle.</p><p>Frozen limits: beam/channel force 0.1 N; contact/strength and attributable float32 contact rounding 0.25 N; rest/state 10 µm; velocity 2 µm/s; per-step world-position envelope 150 µm; combined aggregate force/momentum/kinetic parity 1e-5; storage/event ports 0.001 J; impulse/work residuals 0.001 in their respective units. Identity/counts must agree exactly. The contact rounding envelope applies to an approximately 0.8 MN float32 accumulation; previous contactless fixture limits are unchanged.</p>',image('impact-yield-v1-qualification.png','Actual React scoped qualification: measured discrepancies and the frozen limits.'),'<h2>Repeatability and required loss</h2><p>Three fresh processes per fixture have bitwise identical complete dense payloads and aggregate physics records with the wall timer excluded. Each healthy window has ticks 1,202–13,202 inclusive (12,001 frames), with all nodes, 16 channels, beams and populated contacts at 2 kHz. All seven original analytical/initialization fixtures reran and passed unchanged limits.</p><p>Queue-overflow injection at tick 5,702 and partial-write injection at tick 5,202 each omit one required frame while retaining later detail through tick 13,202. Both finish execution with Incomplete capture and NotReady science; independent successors continue. These injections do not qualify actual physical disk exhaustion.</p>',image('required-loss.png','Sticky loss remains visible after writers close; later observations are retained.'),'<h2>Authoring and retained inspection</h2><p>The workbench exposes both frozen scenarios, guards pinned inputs, shows the contact/change/removal sequence, pages the verified transition ledger and inspects exact retained native ticks. UI checks exercised a real source worker authored through React, live recorder health, both archived sequences/ledgers, exact transition-tick queries, sticky loss, mobile layout and browser errors.</p>',image('impact-fracture-v1-sequence.png','Actual retained removal sequence and complete detail coverage.'),image('impact-yield-v1-ledger.png','Actual native transitions and signed storage ports in the workbench.')]
parts+=['<h2>Build, provenance and retained failures</h2><p>Fresh Windows x64 Release native output: VS 2022/MSVC 19.44, CMake/Ninja, six parallel jobs and the existing Conan dependency cache. Native CTest passed 2/2; locked managed builds and production React pass. All '+str(summary['nativeProcesses'])+' native processes use the new source executable and private DLLs. '+str(summary['nativeInputs'])+' native/CMake input hashes match; build input was dirty beyond HEAD '+source['head']+'. Exact inputs remain independent of later Git publication.</p><p>Executable SHA-256: <code>'+build['sha256']+'</code>.</p><p>Native reader checks include CRC-valid adversaries that alter kind, storage port, force epoch, contact normal, velocity or strength. They remain valid byte captures and cannot pass science. An initial epoch=999 adversary was rejected at the integrity reader rather than the intended semantic gate; epoch=1 exercises the semantic failure correctly. Failed test directories/logs are retained. UI testing found duplicate sibling React keys that accumulated inspector/ledger panels when switching attempts; distinct keys fix the issue. A subsequent test reused an old authoring name and failed to select the fresh run; unique names repair the harness. All resulting native attempts remain retained.</p>', '<h2>Resource and retention boundaries</h2><p>This four-node detail profile uses '+f"{selected[0]['profile']['historyBytes']/2**20:.2f}"+' MiB history and a 64 MiB queue, approximately '+f"{selected[0]['rawWindowBytes']/2**20:.2f}"+' MiB per healthy window. It is distinct from the unchanged Daf profile (~782 MiB history, 3 GiB queue, ~1.55 GB/window). Rates/windows and wire layouts are unchanged. Existing conservative 6 GiB available-memory and 10 GiB + 3 GiB disk preflight gates apply to impact launches.</p><p>The new build, archives, failed harness outputs and media live in <code>'+html.escape(str(root))+'</code>. C: was selected to preserve D: storage and every previous recorded original. No original evidence or installed-game files were removed. Continuous native image capture was enabled, so this slice is not a performance-budget benchmark.</p>', '<h2>Native scene and playable evidence</h2><p>Eighteen unmodified RoR renderer PNGs provide a nominal 2 fps video and 36 nonblank decoded image samples. Visible WebM pixels and ordinary-image progression pass in system Chrome; Codex GPU playback remains unverified. The presentation clock differs from the physics clock. This small fixture’s native follow camera can obscure the beam near the box; archive plots and exact tick inspection establish the transition outcome.</p>',image('native-scene.png','Genuine native render-window capture from the new source-built two-mass removal worker.'),'<iframe title="Native renderer video and ordinary-image player" src="'+url(media/'playback/playback.html')+'"></iframe>', '<div class="links">'+link(media/'playback/playback.html','Open image/video player')+link(root/'report/results.json','Measured results')+link(root/'report/slice-07-review.zip','Portable review bundle')+link(repo/'apps/trials/impact-fixture-format.md','Fixture/reference contract')+'</div><h2>Remaining work</h2><p>Full vehicle constitutive/environmental energy closure, calibrated material damage/dissipation, nonlinear beams, arbitrary topologies and larger/retriggered impacts remain unqualified. This closes the controlled later-transition gap; it does not promote the Daf vehicle to scientifically Passed. Broader energy/environment work and workload performance qualification remain the next engineering areas.</p><footer>Session 2026-10-10, America/New_York. Development/integration stays on dev; periodic master promotion is user-managed.</footer></main></body></html>']
(repo/'doc/project/reports/trial-slice-07-2026-10-10.html').write_text(''.join(parts),encoding='utf-8');print(json.dumps({k:summary[k] for k in ['nativeSha256','nativeInputs','nativeProcesses','outcomes']}))
